ports `metis`).\n    \n    `export METIS_URL=https://metis.internal:8080   # default http://127.0.0.1:8080\n    export AIFACTORY_METIS_GATE=auto               # auto | on | off (default auto)\n    export AIFACTORY_METIS_GATE_BLOCK=0          # 1 = allow low-confidence to escalate\n    `\n\nFull env table + sequence diagrams: `docs/metis-integration.md` · RU · ES · FR · ZH\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/alexar76/aimarket-mcp/tree)\nciteturn63search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago;     | `AIMARKET_METIS_URL` | Metis verify API base (default `https://metis.modelmarket.dev`) |\n      # input JSON with device_id om-wx-01 — see tool schema / hub docs\n    )\n    ```\n    \n    Or the same HTTP the tool wraps:\n    \n    ```bash\n    curl -s -X POST \"${AIMARKET_HUB_URL:-https://modelmarket.dev}/ai-market/v2/invoke\" \\\n      -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n      -H 'X-AIMarket-Sandbox-Visitor: vis_mcp_om_wx' \\\n      -d '{\"capability_id\":\"gaia.weather.read@v1\",\"product_id\":\"gaia.gateway\",\n           \"source_hub\":\"https://iot.modelmarket.dev\",\"input\":{\"device_id\":\"om-wx-01\"}}'\n    ```\n    \n    That is the **easy** path (trial/sandbox). Proving an **external wallet** paid on-chain\n    is a separate escrow flow (`openChannel` → DebitAuthorization → hub debit/settle) —\n    see [`docs/onchain-journal.md`](https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/docs/onchain-journal.md) §3l–§3m and\n    [`gaia/docs/LIVE-RELAYS.md`](https://github.com/alexar76/gaia/blob/main/docs/LIVE-RELAYS.md).\n    \n    Why a gateway (not per-agent tools): generic capabilities are written **once**; the security core lives in one audited place. Ecosystem-specific capabilities live in their own MCP servers (`aimarket-oracle-gateway`, `aimarket-plugins`).\n    \n    ## Configure (env)\n    \n    | var | meaning |\n    |-----|---------|\n    | `AIMARKET_METIS_URL` | Metis verify API base (default `https://metis.modelmarket.dev`) |\n    | `AIMARKET_METIS_KEY` | optional bearer for Metis verify |\n    | `AIMARKET_SEARCH_URL` | DuckDuckGo HTML endpoint override |\n    | `AIMARKET_HUB_URL` | AIMarket hub for `market_search` / `market_invoke` (default `https://modelmarket.dev`) |\n    | `AIMARKET_API_KEY` | Credit-account key from the hub's `/start` page (`https://modelmarket.dev/start`): priced `market_invoke` calls are paid from its prepaid balance; while it is short the free trial still applies. In HTTP mode it pays for every caller of that server |\n    | `AIMARKET_SANDBOX_VISITOR` | Trial identity for `market_invoke`; random per install, set it to keep an allowance across reinstalls |\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAIMarket MCP MCP Server – Features, Use Cases, Setup & Alternatives - MCP.Pub (https://mcp.pub/servers/aimarket-mcp/)\nciteturn63search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; aimarket-mcp is an ecosystem MCP gateway that provides web fetch, web search, and Metis verification capabilities behind one SSRF-hardened endpoint.\n\n# AIMarket MCP\n\naimarket-mcp updated 2026-07-11 Active MCP.Pub 6.5\n\nEnables web fetching, web search, and Metis verification for AI agents via a single MCP endpoint.\n\naimarket-mcp is an ecosystem MCP gateway that provides web fetch, web search, and Metis verification capabilities behind one SSRF-hardened endpoint.\n\n## What it does\n\n  * web_fetch – Fetches a URL and returns main text with SSRF protection and output sanitization.\n  * web_search – Performs live web searches via DuckDuckGo and returns top snippets.\n  * metis_verify – Runs Metis cognition and verification on input, returning a verification score.\n\n## Setup notes\n\n  * Install via `pip install -e .` or `docker compose up -d`.\n  * Requires environment variables: `AIMARKET_MCP_KEY` (bearer token), `AIMARKET_MCP_PRODUCTION=1` for production mode.\n  * Optional: `AIMARKET_MCP_PORT`, `AIMARKET_MCP_RATE`, `AIMARKET_METIS_URL`, `AIMARKET_METIS_KEY`, `AIMARKET_SEARCH_URL`.\n\n## Security and limitations\n\nSSRF-hardened (scheme allowlist, private-IP block, per-redirect re-validation, size cap); output sanitized and wrapped in <untrusted> tags; optional bearer auth (fail-closed in production); rate limit per-key/IP token bucket (default 120/min).\n\n## Editorial verdict\n\nMCP.Pub reviewed this listing with a quality score of 6.5/10 based on the collected public evidence.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAIMarket MCP Gateway MCP Server | PluginBench (https://pluginbench.com/mcp/io.github.alexar76/aimarket-mcp)\nciteturn63search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month;   * `AIMARKET_METIS_URL`\n\nPluginBenchMCP ServersAIMarket MCP Gateway\n\nMCP Server\n\nActive\n\nMIT\n\n# AIMarket MCP Gateway MCP Server\n\nio.github.alexar76/aimarket-mcp\n\nRepositoryRegistry\n\n## What is the AIMarket MCP Gateway MCP server?\n\nStdio + HTTP MCP gateway: SSRF-hardened web_fetch, web_search, metis_verify, market_search.\n\n## How to install AIMarket MCP Gateway\n\nCopy-paste configuration for popular MCP clients.\n\ntransport: stdio\n\nConfig generated by PluginBench — verify against the source before use.\n\nEnvironment / auth\n\n  * `AIMARKET_METIS_URL`\n\nMetis verify API base URL\n\n  * `AIMARKET_METIS_KEY`\n\nsecret\n\nOptional bearer token for Metis verify\n\n  * `AIMARKET_SEARCH_URL`\n\nDuckDuckGo HTML search endpoint override\n\n  * `Authorization`\n\nsecret\n\nBearer token matching AIMARKET_MCP_KEY when auth is enabled\n\nClaude Desktop Cursor Windsurf VS Code Claude Code\n\n~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json\n\nCopy\n    \n    `{\n      \"mcpServers\": {\n        \"aimarket-mcp\": {\n          \"command\": \"uvx\",\n          \"args\": [\n            \"aimarket-mcp\"\n          ],\n          \"env\": {\n            \"AIMARKET_METIS_URL\": \"<YOUR_AIMARKET_METIS_URL>\",\n            \"AIMARKET_METIS_KEY\": \"<YOUR_AIMARKET_METIS_KEY>\",\n            \"AIMARKET_SEARCH_URL\": \"<YOUR_AIMARKET_SEARCH_URL>\",\n            \"Authorization\": \"<YOUR_AUTHORIZATION>\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }`\n\n## Popularity & trust\n\nStars\n\n1 (1)\n\nForks\n\n2\n\nOpen issues\n\n5\n\nLanguage\n\nPython\n\nLicense\n\nMIT\n\nLast commit\n\n2026-08-16\n\nVersion\n\n0.3.0--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSchema | aimarket-mcp | Glama (https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/alexar76/aimarket-mcp/schema)\nciteturn63search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 weeks ago; `AIMARKET_METIS_KEY`  | No  | API key for the Metis verification service.\n\nImage: alexar76\n\n## aimarket-mcp\n\nBrowser AutomationSearchAgent Orchestration\n\nby alexar76\n\nPython\n\nRemote\n\n### Server Configuration\n\nDescribes the environment variables required to run the server.\n\nName  | Required  | Description  | Default\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n`AIMARKET_MCP_KEY`  | No  | Optional bearer token for authentication. Required if AIMARKET_MCP_PRODUCTION is set to 1.  | \n`AIMARKET_MCP_PORT`  | No  | Port to listen on (default: 9090).  | \n`AIMARKET_MCP_RATE`  | No  | Rate limit per key/IP (default: 120/min).  | \n`AIMARKET_METIS_KEY`  | No  | API key for the Metis verification service.  | \n`AIMARKET_METIS_URL`  | No  | URL for the Metis verification service (required for metis_verify tool).  | \n`AIMARKET_SEARCH_URL`  | No  | URL for the search service (required for web_search tool).  | \n`AIMARKET_MCP_PRODUCTION`  | No  | Set to '1' to enable production mode, which requires AIMARKET_MCP_KEY.  | \n\n### Instructions\n\nGuidance the server publishes about itself, which clients place ahead of the tool catalog so the model reads it before choosing anything.\n\nThis server publishes no instructions, or was last inspected before Glama recorded them.\n\n### Capabilities\n\nFeatures and capabilities supported by this server\n\nProtocol revision`2025-11-25`\n\nCapability  | Details\n--- | ---\n`tools`  | \n    \n    {\n      \"listChanged\": false\n    }\n\n`prompts`  | \n    \n    {\n      \"listChanged\": false\n    }\n\n`resources`  | \n    \n    {\n      \"subscribe\": false,\n      \"listChanged\": false\n    }\n\n`experimental`  | \n    \n    {}\n\n### Tools\n\nFunctions exposed to the LLM to take actions\n\nName  | Description\n--- | ---\nweb_fetch_toolA  | Fetch a web page by URL and return its main text content.SSRF-hardened (scheme allow-list, private-IP block, per-redirect re-validation, size cap). Output is sanitized, role-marker stripped, and wrapped in `<untrusted>…</untrusted>` before it can reach a model — safe for agent consumption with explicit untrusted marking.\nweb_search_toolA  | Search the web for current facts and return the top result snippets.Uses DuckDuckGo HTML results. Output is sanitized and wrapped `<untrusted>` like web_fetch. Prefer this over guessing when the answer depends on recent events or documentation.\nmetis_verify_toolA  | Run Metis cognition + verification on an input; returns answer plus verify_score/verified.Calls the Metis `/v1/verify` API. Response includes machine-readable metadata `[verify_score=… status=… route=… verified=…]` so agents can fail-closed when confidence is insufficient. Configure AIMARKET_METIS_URL and optional AIMARKET_METIS_KEY.\n\n### Prompts\n\nInteractive templates invoked by user choice\n\nName  | Description\n--- | ---\nNo prompts\n\n### Resources\n\nContextual data attached and managed by the client\n\nName  | Description\n--- | ---\nNo resources\n\n  * PyPI Package\n  * GitHub Repository\nNeed Help?Report IssueRelated Servers--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\naimarket-hub · PyPI (https://pypi.org/project/aimarket-hub/)\nciteturn63search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 days ago; Crawled: today; `AIMARKET_VERIFY_MAX_CONCURRENCY`  | `8`  | Cap on simultaneous Metis calls across pending settlements\n`AIMARKET_VERIFY_FAIL_CLOSED`  | `1`  | Indeterminate outcome ⇒ refund the buyer. Only an explicit `0/false/no/off` captures instead; an unrecognised value is a typo and still fails closed\n`AIMARKET_VERIFY_METIS_URL`  | `http://127.0.0.1:8080`  | Metis base URL (falls back to `METIS_URL`)\n`AIMARKET_VERIFY_METIS_KEY`  | —  | Metis bearer key (falls back to `METIS_API_KEY`)\n`AIMARKET_VERIFY_VERIFIER_ID`  | `metis.verify@v1`  | Envelope `verifier` attribution when a non-Metis verifier serves the slot\n`AIMARKET_APPEAL_WINDOW_S`  | `0`  | Appeals (protocol): seconds a genuine paid verdict stays provisional and appealable by the losing party. `0` = off, verdicts move money at once\n`AIMARKET_APPEAL_METIS_URL`  | —  | The appeal court: a second verifier. Unset, or equal to the first-instance URL, keeps appeals off\n`AIMARKET_APPEAL_METIS_KEY`  | —  | Appeal court bearer key\n`AIMARKET_APPEAL_VERIFIER_ID`  | `metis.appeal@v1`  | Names the appeal court in envelopes; must differ from `AIMARKET_VERIFY_VERIFIER_ID`\n`AIMARKET_APPEAL_BOND_MIN_USD` / `AIMARKET_APPEAL_BOND_RATE`  | `0.02` / `0.20`  | Bond = max(min, rate × price), capped at the price\n`AIMARKET_APPEAL_MAX_WAIT_S`  | `21600`  | After this the court counts as indeterminate: the first verdict stands, the bond is returned (`0` = no limit)\n`AIMARKET_APPEAL_SWEEP_S`  | `30`  | Safety-net pass that finalizes expired windows and picks up filed appeals\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAIMarket MCP Gateway (https://tracevero.com/mcp/io-github-alexar76-aimarket-mcp)\nciteturn63search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Environment variables (raw)  | AIMARKET_METIS_URL, AIMARKET_METIS_KEY, AIMARKET_SEARCH_URL, AIMARKET_API_KEY Source: MCP-Register · collected on 2026-10-08 · self-declared\n\nSource data 25\n\nEvidence for this page: The values on this page come from several collections. Each row therefore states its own origin.\n\nRaw values\nDescription (raw)  | Stdio + H